findings.detail:
APIs: android.graphics.RuntimeShader (API 33, @RequiresApi(Build.VERSION_CODES.TIRAMISU)) wrapped in androidx.compose.ui.graphics.ShaderBrush. Create the shader ONCE in Modifier.drawWithCache, push uniforms and drawRect(brush) in onDrawBehind. Official docs use ValueAnimator for time; the idiomatic Compose driver is produceState + androidx.compose.animation.core.withInfiniteAnimationFrameMillis (respects the animation clock, auto-pauses when not composed — good for battery).

Driver:
@Composable fun rememberShaderTime(): State<Float> = produceState(0f) {
  val start = withFrameMillis { it }
  while (true) { withInfiniteAnimationFrameMillis { value = (it - start) / 1000f } }
}

Usage (note: read timeState.value INSIDE onDrawBehind so only the draw phase invalidates):
val timeState = rememberShaderTime()
Box(Modifier.fillMaxSize().drawWithCache {
  val shader = RuntimeShader(AURA_AGSL)
  shader.setFloatUniform("iResolution", size.width, size.height)
  val brush = ShaderBrush(shader)
  onDrawBehind {
    shader.setFloatUniform("iTime", timeState.value)
    shader.setFloatUniform("iProgress", progress)   // 0..1 across the interval
    shader.setColorUniform("deep", android.graphics.Color.valueOf(r,g,b,a))
    shader.setColorUniform("bright", android.graphics.Color.valueOf(r,g,b,a))
    drawRect(brush)
  }
})

Minimal slow multi-color flow shader (@Language("AGSL") String). Feed a hue/progress uniform to move deep->bright green (work) or blue (rest):
uniform float2 iResolution; uniform float iTime; uniform float iProgress;
layout(color) uniform half4 deep; layout(color) uniform half4 bright;
half4 main(float2 fragCoord){
  float2 uv = fragCoord/iResolution;
  float t = iTime*0.15;
  float flow  = 0.5+0.5*sin(uv.x*3.0+t)*cos(uv.y*2.0-t*0.7);
  float flow2 = 0.5+0.5*sin((uv.x+uv.y)*2.5-t*1.3);
  half4 base = mix(deep, bright, flow);
  base = mix(base, bright, flow2*0.35);
  base = mix(deep, base, iProgress);   // deep at interval start -> bright at end
  return base;
}
Swap deep/bright between green and blue palettes for work vs rest; cross-fade the two uniform sets with animateColorAsState on transitions. Uniform names must match exactly; color uniforms need android.graphics.Color.valueOf() (or setColorUniform). Below API 33 the fallback is Brush.verticalGradient/linearGradient animated with rememberInfiniteTransition — but see device finding: not needed here.

Draw in a Modifier.drawWithCache/drawBehind over the aura. Build a closed rounded-rect Path inset to the safe area with the device corner radius, measure it with androidx.compose.ui.graphics.PathMeasure, and carve out the leading 0..1 fraction with getSegment.

Compose PathMeasure API (androidx.compose.ui.graphics.PathMeasure): fun setPath(path: Path?, forceClosed: Boolean); val length: Float; fun getSegment(startDistance: Float, stopDistance: Float, destination: Path, startWithMoveTo: Boolean = true): Boolean.

Modifier.drawWithCache {
  val inset = safeInsetPx        // from displayCutout + a margin
  val r = deviceCornerRadiusPx  // from WindowInsets.getRoundedCorner (finding 4)
  val path = Path().apply { addRoundRect(RoundRect(inset, inset, size.width-inset, size.height-inset, CornerRadius(r,r))) }
  val pm = PathMeasure().apply { setPath(path, /*forceClosed=*/true) }
  val total = pm.length
  val dst = Path()
  onDrawBehind {
    dst.rewind()
    pm.getSegment(0f, total * progress, dst, true)   // progress = 0..1 for the interval
    drawPath(dst, color = accent, style = Stroke(width = 8.dp.toPx(), cap = StrokeCap.Round))
  }
}

GLOW: cheapest true glow is drawIntoCanvas + android.graphics.Paint with a BlurMaskFilter (needs setLayerType/hardware caveat) OR — simpler and hardware-accelerated — draw the stroke twice: a wide low-alpha stroke on a graphicsLayer whose renderEffect is a blur (API 31+), with the crisp stroke on top. Since it traces a start->end progress arc, start the segment at 12 o'clock by rotating the path or offsetting the start distance.

GOTCHA: older Compose PathMeasure had a caching bug where getSegment returned stale results unless setPath was re-called; on current stable it's fine, but re-run setPath whenever size/inset/radius changes (i.e., keep it inside drawWithCache which re-caches on size change) and rewind() the destination path each frame.
